From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Opz Browser <opz@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:28:05 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Containers: sync containers and their sites through Sync's
 settings

Firefox Sync has no container engine. OpzContainerSync writes the containers
(name, icon, color) and the site-to-container choices into the pref
opz.containers.sync, which prefs/opz.js marks syncable, so it travels with
Settings sync; an incoming value is merged back per container and per site,
newest change first. Removed containers leave a tombstone so they are removed
on the other devices too. Containers that exist on both sides before the first
sync are matched by name. Private-tab containers have no identity and are not
synced; the order of containers is not synced.
---
 browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest |   1 +
 browser/modules/OpzContainerSync.sys.mjs      | 415 ++++++++++++++++++
 browser/modules/moz.build                     |   1 +
 3 files changed, 417 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 browser/modules/OpzContainerSync.sys.mjs

diff --git a/browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest b/browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest
